From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 19:41:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sunxi-ng: a733: Keep the PLL N factor within the
 manual's range

PLL_DDR, PLL_PERI0, PLL_PERI1, PLL_VIDEO0 to PLL_VIDEO2, PLL_VE0,
PLL_VE1, PLL_NPU and PLL_DE take N = PLL_N + 1 from bits 15:8. The A733
manual limits the field in each of them: PLL_N is from 0 to 254 and no
less than 11, so N runs from 12 to 255. The driver allows N from 11 to
256, so a rate search can pick N = 11, and N = 256 writes a field value
the manual does not allow.

Limit N to 12..255 for these PLLs, as already done for the audio PLLs.
The reset values of all ten PLLs lie inside this range.

Not covered: PLL_GPU0 keeps its tighter limit from its VCO range, and
the VCO ranges of the other PLLs are not enforced.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: rate requests beyond both ends on VIDEO0/1/2,
DE, VE0, VE1 and NPU gave N 12 and 255 instead of 11 and 256; not tested
on DDR, PERI0 and PERI1, which are in use.

Assisted-by: LLM
